# Build output
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.log
*.pid

# Doom-engine WAD data files are id Software's copyrighted content (even the
# freely-redistributable shareware episode has its own distribution terms) —
# never commit them. Supply your own locally; see game_design.txt.
#
# testdata/DOOM1.WAD is a deliberate, local-only exception used by the
# automated tests (wad/wad_test.go, bsp/bsp_test.go) — it's still excluded
# here in case this project is ever pushed to a shared/public remote.
*.wad
*.WAD

# Runtime-loaded image assets are never committed (see game_design.txt
# sections 10-11, 18): the skybox and the hi-res wall/flat/sprite override
# set are generated by tools/gensky / tools/gentex, or supplied locally by
# dropping a third-party pack in. Same reasoning as the WADs above — a
# hi-res "texture pack" is a derivative of id Software's copyrighted art
# and carries its own terms.
/assets/skybox/
/assets/textures/

# Voxel model packs (e.g. Cheello's Voxel Doom) are a derivative of id
# Software's copyrighted sprites and carry their own terms — supply your own
# locally in assets/voxel/ (Doom1_Voxel.pk3 / Doom2_Voxel.pk3). See
# game_design.txt section 20.
/assets/voxel/*.pk3
/assets/voxel/*.PK3

# HD weapon viewmodel pack — same reasoning: a derivative of id's sprites,
# supplied locally in assets/weapons/ as a .pk3. See game_design.txt
# section 11.
/assets/weapons/

# Raw third-party packs waiting to be imported (e.g. a Quake 1 texture .pk3
# for tools/importquake). Same "supply your own locally" story — often
# hundreds of MB and not ours to redistribute. The converted output lands
# under /assets/textures/ which is already excluded above.
/assets/import/

# Drop-in mod folder (GLDEFS / brightmap / texture packs — .pk3s or loose
# files). Third-party content, supplied locally. The example GLDEFS and the
# folder README are the only tracked files here.
/assets/mods/*
!/assets/mods/GLDEFS.example
!/assets/mods/UMAPINFO.example
!/assets/mods/ANIMDEFS.example
!/assets/mods/TEXTURES.example
!/assets/mods/README.txt

# Auto-installed local tooling (shader compiler, etc.) — not committed.
/.tooling/
